      <xs:documentation>Indicates how the caller expects errors be handled. If this is 'Caller', then the caller is expected to be responsible for handling an error response.  If this is set to 'Central', then the error is triaged by a central error handler. The central error handler tries to fix the error, and if it cannot be fixed, notifies the appropriate caller. When using this option, it is important that CallingProcessIdentifier is completed so that the central error triage process can route the error accordingly.</xs:documentation>
